          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a journey of 15 km, the total amount paid is ₹220. What is the fixed charge and the charge per km? How much does a person have to pay for travelling a distance of 25 km?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.178,
            0.882,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) A fraction becomes equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 9 } { 1 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " if 2 is added to both the numerator and the denominator. If 3 is added to both the numerator and the denominator, it becomes equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 6 } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the fraction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.293,
            0.882,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) If we add 1 to the numerator and subtract 1 from the denominator, a fraction reduces to 1. It becomes equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\mathrm { i f }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we add 1 only to the denominator. What is the fraction?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.371,
            0.881,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vii) Five years ago, Nuri was thrice as old as Sonu. Ten years later, Nuri will be twice as old as Sonu. How old are Nuri and Sonu?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.409,
            0.882,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(viii) The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 9. Also, nine times this number is twice the number obtained by reversing the order of the digits. Find the number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.467,
            0.882,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ix) Meena went to a bank to withdraw ₹2000. She asked the cashier to give her ₹50 and ₹100 notes only. Meena got 25 notes in all. Find how many notes of ₹50 and ₹100 did she receive?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.544,
            0.882,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(x) A lending library has a fixed charge for the first three days and an additional charge for each day thereafter. Saritha paid ₹27 for a book kept for seven days, while Susy paid ₹21 for the book she kept for five days. Find the fixed charge and the charge for each extra day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.65,
            0.881,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Form a pair of linear equations and find their common solutions graphically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
